<p>Nepal began counting votes on March 6 after a generally peaceful parliamentary election the day before—the country’s first national vote since Gen Z-led protests forced the then prime minister to step down and triggered early elections. Early returns across several outlets showed the newly formed Rastriya Swatantra Party (RSP) ahead in dozens of constituencies, with its prominent candidate Balendra (Balen) Shah—described as a rapper-turned-politician and former Kathmandu mayor—performing strongly in the initial count. Election officials put early turnout at about 60%. Indian outlets highlighted the scale of the operation across 77 districts, with thousands of polling centres and polling stations. Many reports framed the race as a choice between established parties and a youth-driven demand for new leadership, noting young voters’ hopes for jobs and cleaner governance as labour migration remains high. With counting still underway, the big questions are whether the early RSP lead holds and what coalition arithmetic follows. For now, the calm vote offers a brighter sign of civic participation after months of political upheaval.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/0q0_0B_POj2BhsFHZVCUoXw4kXT4Bjz7MqBbnwTgt5QLPtrDur7ubP1NsEf4jWFmrG22tYHH3_myWvjt2s02tKaDGOHl6fvyf0-Guu_Sj_WaRqsflZzkuCXoSmu-NUFXP8mHrvps1BZaNZNnyS4wAt23TIpqH_bHbtff7YSdqbFOH31m7aT9MNU0df4hnKfr7PV_JxuA6FsE6snlsSkeWw' alt='Voting in Kathmandu, Nepal, on Thursday.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Turnout snapshot: Officials and preliminary estimates put voter turnout at around 60%, with one outlet calling it the lowest in more than two decades.</li><li>Key matchup: In Jhapa-5, early counts cited by Indian media showed Balendra Shah ahead of former Prime Minister K.P. Sharma Oli (10,190 votes to 4,087 at the time of that report).</li><li>Seats at stake: Voters elected 275 seats in the House of Representatives, according to AP’s election coverage.</li><li>Youth migration pressure: Le Monde reported that more than 2,000 young Nepalis leave the country each day for work abroad, a backdrop shaping what many younger voters want from the election.</li><li>Early lead picture: Early counting updates showed the RSP leading in 47 constituencies in initial trends/updates.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Election Commission (Chief election commissioner Ram Prasad Bhandari): Bhandari said voting concluded peacefully as officials began sharing early turnout estimates. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/05/nepal-election-2026-voting-balen-shah-sharma-oli'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Rastriya Swatantra Party supporters/young voters (as described by outlets): Coverage said the RSP and Balendra Shah are drawing strong backing from younger voters who want a break from the old guard and a shift in governance priorities. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/05/world/asia/gen-z-nepal-election.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>Nepali youth affected by job shortages: Le Monde reported that many young people are hoping the election brings new economic momentum as unemployment fuels large-scale labour migration. (<a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/03/05/nepal-s-youth-long-forced-abroad-for-work-look-to-elections-for-fresh-start_6751135_4.html'>Le Monde</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/vote-counting-begins-nepal-after-peaceful-parliamentary-election-130815186'>Vote counting begins in Nepal after a peaceful parliamentary election</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/nepal-election-2026-results-live-updates-balendra-shah-gagan-thapa-kp-sharma-oli-nepal-to-count-votes-shortly-for-first-polls-held-after-gen-z-protest-11175123#publisher=newsstand'>Nepal Election 2026 Results Live Updates: Balen Shah&#x27;s Rastriya Swatantra Party Leads In 47 Constituencies</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.firstpost.com/explainers/nepal-election-results-balen-shah-prime-minister-gen-z-protests-13986781.html'>After the Gen-Z revolution, is Nepal set to get a rapper PM in Balen Shah?</a> - firstpost.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/05/world/asia/gen-z-nepal-election.html'>After Gen-Z Revolution, Nepal Votes for a Fresh Slate of Leaders</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/03/05/nepal-s-youth-long-forced-abroad-for-work-look-to-elections-for-fresh-start_6751135_4.html'>Nepal&#x27;s youth, long forced abroad for work, look to elections for fresh start</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/nepal-election-result-counting-rsp-nepali-congress-cpn-uml-updates/article70710001.ece'>Nepal election results: RSP leading in 47 constituencies</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/05/nepal-election-2026-voting-balen-shah-sharma-oli'>Nepal: voting closes in election pitting old guard against powerful youth movement</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://apnews.com/article/nepal-shah-oli-protests-election-58cac72e25490c8c6363626a7dc10171'>Nepalis vote to elect 275 seats of the House of Representatives nearly six months after the Gen Z protests.</a> - apnews.com</li></ul>